submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(x for row in grid for x in row)\n    bg = counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n\n    # Find the embedded three-cell pattern.\n    pattern = None\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w - 2):\n            vals = grid[r][c:c+3]\n            if all(v != bg for v in vals) and len(set(vals)) == 3:\n                pattern = (\"h\", r, c, vals[:])\n                break\n        if pattern:\n            break\n    if pattern is None:\n        for r in range(h - 2):\n            for c in range(w):\n                vals = [grid[r+i][c] for i in range(3)]\n                if all(v != bg for v in vals) and len(set(vals)) == 3:\n                    pattern = (\"v\", r, c, vals)\n                    break\n            if pattern:\n                break\n\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    if pattern is None:\n        return out\n\n    orient, pr, pc, vals = pattern\n    # The sparse marker color is the non-background color occurring most often.\n    marker = max((v for v in counts if v != bg), key=lambda v: counts[v])\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if grid[r][c] != marker:\n                continue\n            if orient == \"h\":\n                for k, v in enumerate(vals):\n                    cc = c + k - 1\n                    if 0 <= cc < w:\n                        out[r][cc] = v\n            else:\n                for k, v in enumerate(vals):\n                    rr = r + k - 1\n                    if 0 <= rr < h:\n                        out[rr][c] = v\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":39,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1790608278.245,"t1":1790608291.455,"alias":"task-e2153329","message":"Your program was checked on earlier pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n0 